  "body": "Add a guide section on machine types: what each one is, how CamCraft treats it, and how the choice changes setups, operations, tools and posting. Today the guide has a short \"Machines\" heading in `setups.md`; a user choosing or switching a machine needs more.\n\nOne page or section per type, each covering the same points:\n- **Milling (VMC, 3-axis and 4th/5th axis, tilt-head).** The default. Rotary axes and what they unlock (rotary and multi-axis operations); travel and reach limits.\n- **Routers** (gantry routers and desktop machines, which CamCraft models as mills). What differs in practice: large shallow work, sheet goods, spoilboard and hold-down, higher rpm with smaller tools, tabs, Z-zero on the spoilboard vs on the stock.\n- **Turning (lathe).** The work spindle turns the part; the turning operation family; X as diameter; chucks and the workholding rpm limit; what's refused on a lathe (milling operations, off-centre holes).\n- **Mill-turn.** Both spindles: turning sections on the work spindle, live tooling on the tool spindle (C-axis); how a setup and a post pick between them; the dialect line in the post script (`capabilities`, #1199).\n- **Plasma.** A tool-less cut: no spindle, kerf, pierce, torch height, which operations exist (plasma profile) and which are refused.\n- **EDM: wire and sinker.** Electrodes and wire instead of cutters, conditions (gap, wire diameter, undersize), no spindle; what ships now and what's still coming (#533 / #542 posts). Write the section once those ship, or mark it \"in progress\".\n\nFor every type, include a small table of which operation families are allowed, what the setup needs (stock, WCS, workholding), the posts that ship for it, and the common refusals (link the troubleshooting page, #1244). Also: what happens when a setup's machine is switched (operations are judged against the new machine at post; see #1254).\n\nTake the operation-to-machine rules from the code (`Family::admits`, the posting family and lathe doors), not from memory.\n\nDone means: a machine types section in the guide covering mill, router, lathe, mill-turn, plasma and EDM, each with allowed operations, setup needs, shipped posts and common refusals, linked from setups.md.\n",
